<% const full = markdown.full; %>
<details class="markdown-help">
  <summary><%= full ? 'Full Markdown is supported' : 'Limited Markdown is supported' %></summary>
  <div class="markdown-help-body">
    <p class="fineprint">Anything not listed as supported is shown exactly as you typed it. Put a backslash before a marker (<code>\*</code>) to keep it literal.</p>
    <h2 class="markdown-help-subhead">Supported</h2>
    <dl class="markdown-help-list">
      <div><dt><code>**bold**</code></dt><dd><strong>bold</strong></dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>*italics*</code> or <code>_italics_</code></dt><dd><em>italics</em></dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>__underline__</code></dt><dd><u>underline</u></dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>~~strikethrough~~</code></dt><dd><s>strikethrough</s></dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>`code`</code></dt><dd><code>code</code></dd></div>
      <div><dt><code># Title</code> through <code><%= full ? '######' : '###' %> Smallest</code></dt><dd>Headings, one per line</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>- item</code></dt><dd>Bulleted list</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>&gt; quoted</code></dt><dd>Block quote</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Blank line</dt><dd>New paragraph; a single line break stays a line break</dd></div>
      <% if (full) { %>
        <div><dt><code>[label](https://example.com)</code></dt><dd>Hyperlink, HTTPS only</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>1. item</code></dt><dd>Numbered list</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Two spaces of indent</dt><dd>Nested list under the item above</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>```</code> fenced block <code>```</code></dt><dd>Code block, with an optional language after the opening fence</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>| a | b |</code> then <code>| --- | --- |</code></dt><dd>Table, with <code>:---:</code> and <code>---:</code> for centered and right-aligned columns</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>---</code> on its own line</dt><dd>Horizontal rule</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>&lt;https://example.com&gt;</code> or a bare HTTPS URL</dt><dd>Automatic link</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>[label](&lt;https://example.com&gt;)</code></dt><dd>Hyperlink with the address wrapped in angle brackets, the same as a plain one</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>![alt](https://example.com/picture.png)</code></dt><dd>Image from any HTTPS address, or a path on this site</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>- [x] done</code></dt><dd>Task list with ticked and unticked boxes</dd></div>
        <div><dt>A term, then <code>: meaning</code> on the next line</dt><dd>Definition list</dd></div>
        <div><dt><code>text[^1]</code> and <code>[^1]: the note</code></dt><dd>Footnote, collected at the end with a link back</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Headings</dt><dd>Each one gets a link you can copy to point at that section</dd></div>
        <div><dt>HTML tags</dt><dd>Ordinary markup is kept: text, lists, tables, <code>details</code>, <code>img</code>, <code>video</code>, <code>audio</code>, and <code>iframe</code> embeds over HTTPS</dd></div>
      <% } %>
    </dl>
    <h2 class="markdown-help-subhead">Not supported</h2>
    <ul class="markdown-help-list">
      <% if (!full) { %>
        <li>Hyperlinks - write them in the Links section of the profile editor instead. A hyperlink typed into this field is rejected when you save.</li>
        <li>Images, video, and embeds</li>
        <li>Tables, fenced code blocks, and horizontal rules</li>
        <li>Numbered lists and nested lists</li>
        <li>Automatic linking of bare URLs</li>
        <li>Headings deeper than <code>###</code></li>
        <li>Raw HTML - tags are shown as text</li>
      <% } else { %>
        <li>Scripts and anything that runs code: <code>script</code>, <code>object</code>, <code>embed</code>, <code>form</code>, event handlers such as <code>onclick</code>, and <code>javascript:</code> addresses are removed</li>
        <li>Inline <code>style</code> attributes and <code>style</code> blocks, so a profile cannot restyle the site</li>
        <li>Addresses that are not HTTPS or a path on this site</li>
      <% } %>
      <li>Emoji, accented letters, and other non-ASCII characters, including styled "fake font" letters</li>
      <% if (full) { %><li class="fineprint">Anything a viewer's browser loads from another site, such as an embedded video, tells that site the viewer's address. Keep that in mind before embedding.</li><% } %>
    </ul>
    <p class="fineprint">Email addresses you write are automatically hidden behind a click-to-reveal widget.</p>
  </div>
</details>
